    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense looks primed for a productive outing, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill**, our two strongest plays today. **Gunnar Henderson** earns the slate-high score of 81.88, benefiting from a soft matchup against Johnson (5.15 xERA) and the immense leverage of the #2 spot in the order, which maximizes his exposure to high-leverage scoring chances. **Jackson Merrill** follows closely at 75.27; despite facing a tougher hold on the basepaths from the Ritchie battery, his aggressive dynamic platoon advantage against a right-handed starter keeps him as a mandatory anchor for our outfield production. **Andy Pages** also projects exceptionally well (72.83) as he looks to exploit a favorable SP matchup against Rojas, providing a reliable floor for our run-scoring potential.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card was bypassing **Josh Jung** (53.10) for the final utility spots. While **Josh Jung** remains a high-floor asset, he ultimately lost out to the superior efficiency metrics of **Drake Baldwin** and **Coby Mayo** in their respective matchups, as the system prioritized the SP skill differential offered by the Johnson and Peralta pairings. Meanwhile, we are exercising caution with **Dominic Smith**, whose marginal 47.00 score is dampened significantly by a negative L/L platoon split against Peralta. While we are keeping **Nasim Nunez** and **Curtis Mead** on the bench, note that **Nasim Nunez**\u2019s score is depressed by an elite opposing catcher's pop time, effectively neutralizing our internal strategy of prioritizing stolen base efficiency today. Monitor weather reports for any late-breaking developments, though our current alignment provides a balanced blend of power and lineup security against these projected starters.",
